# Team Definitions (GitHub Teams)
# These correspond to GitHub teams that must be configured in the organization

# @senior-engineers - Senior developers across all domains
# @platform-architects - System architects and technical leads  
# @frontend-leads - Frontend team leads and senior frontend engineers
# @backend-leads - Backend team leads and senior backend engineers
# @devops-team - DevOps engineers and infrastructure specialists
# @security-team - Security engineers and security architects
# @qa-engineers - QA engineers and test automation specialists
# @ml-engineers - Machine learning engineers and data scientists
# @ai-engineers - AI specialists and prompt engineers
# @ai-researchers - AI researchers and advanced ML specialists
# @database-admins - Database administrators and data architects
# @api-architects - API design specialists and integration experts
# @ux-designers - UX/UI designers and design system specialists
# @technical-writers - Documentation specialists and content creators
# @product-owners - Product managers and business stakeholders
# @sre-team - Site reliability engineers and monitoring specialists
# @performance-engineers - Performance optimization specialists
# @fintech-specialists - Financial technology domain experts
# @compliance-team - Compliance and regulatory specialists
# @romanian-ai-specialists - Romanian language and cultural AI experts
# @data-engineers - Data engineers and ETL specialists
# @automation-engineers - Test automation and workflow specialists
# @mcp-specialists - Model Context Protocol specialists
# @quantum-specialists - Quantum computing and advanced physics experts
# @cryptography-experts - Cryptography and security protocol specialists
# @design-system-team - Design system maintainers and component specialists
# @cultural-experts - Cultural consultants and localization specialists
# @cto - Chief Technology Officer and executive stakeholders
# @technical-leads - Technical leads across all engineering domains

# Review Requirements:
# - Minimum 2 approvals required for all PRs
# - Security-related changes require 3 approvals including security team
# - Architecture changes require platform architect approval
# - Breaking changes require technical lead approval
# - Release-related changes require product owner approval